@startuml
title 6.6 Diagrama de Secuencia - Validacion de Sesion y Permisos (Flujo Transversal)

actor "Cliente API" as Cliente
participant "routes/provider.py" as Routes
participant "dependencies.py" as Deps
participant "clients.py" as Clients
participant "ms-autenticacion" as AUTH
participant "ms-roles" as ROLES

note over Routes
Cualquier operacion en el microservicio
comienza con validacion
end note

Cliente -> Routes: POST /api/v1/<recurso>\nHeader: Authorization: Bearer <token>
activate Routes

note over Routes
Step 1: Generar request_id
request_id = f"PRV-{timestamp}-{random}"
end note

Routes -> Deps: validar_sesion(request)
activate Deps

note over Deps
Extraer token del header Authorization
end note

Deps -> Clients: AuthClient.validate_session(token)
activate Clients

Clients -> AUTH: POST /api/v1/session/validate\nBody: {token: token}
activate AUTH

note over AUTH
ms-autenticacion valida token
Retorna: usuario_id, role_id, 
nombre, email, etc.
end note

AUTH --> Clients: {usuario_id, role_id, email, ...}
deactivate AUTH

Clients --> Deps: sesion_data
deactivate Clients

alt Token no valido
  Deps --> Routes: HTTPException(401)
  Routes --> Cliente: error: Sesion invalida
  deactivate Deps
  deactivate Routes
else Token valido
  Deps --> Routes: sesion_data {usuario_id, role_id}
  deactivate Deps
  
  note over Routes
  Step 2: Validar permisos
  end note
  
  Routes -> Deps: validar_permiso(sesion, permission_code)
  activate Deps
  
  note over Deps
  permission_code ejemplo: PRV_CREATE_EVALUACION
  end note
  
  Deps -> Clients: RolesClient.validate_permission(role_id, permission_code)
  activate Clients
  
  Clients -> ROLES: POST /api/v1/permisos/validar\nBody: {role_id, permission_code}
  activate ROLES
  
  note over ROLES
  ms-roles verifica si el rol
  tiene permiso para ejecutar operacion
  Retorna: {autorizado: true|false}
  end note
  
  ROLES --> Clients: {autorizado: true|false}
  deactivate ROLES
  
  Clients --> Deps: autorizado_bool
  deactivate Clients
  
  alt Permiso denegado
    Deps --> Routes: HTTPException(403)
    Routes --> Cliente: error: Permiso insuficiente
    deactivate Deps
    deactivate Routes
  else Permiso otorgado
    Deps --> Routes: OK
    deactivate Deps
    
    note over Routes
    Step 3: Permitir ejecucion
    de la logica de negocio
    end note
    
    Routes --> Cliente: procesando solicitud...
    deactivate Routes
  end
end

note right of Cliente
Flujo aplicable a TODAS las operaciones:
GET, POST, PUT, DELETE en cualquier recurso
end note

@enduml
